#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
Make this fully grammatical egyptian of the ~1300 BC era.

	𓅓𓎡!

	𓈖𓃀𓇋 𓈖 𓂋𓐍

    𓐍𓏏 𓈖𓃀𓏏 𓅓 𓉐𓏤!

	𓂧𓇋 𓐍𓏏 𓈖𓃀𓏏 𓅓 𓂝𓇋! 𓂺

I want it to be grammatical, but to permit a very clear double reading where the Hebrew original is a plausible MISTRANSLATION from the even earlier excited egyptian.

The joke should be that Joseph had sex with her and was excited, but the Hebrew original is a euphemistic re-reading.

So it should translate as VERY NEARLY THE HEBREW AND ENGLISH ORIGINAL, but it should also actually mean. "Hell yeah! He doesn't know anything! Let me grab 'em" in double meaning space.

Here's the current version:

\Verse{7}
{
	\hJ{וַיְהִי אַחַר הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה וַתִּשָּׂא אֵשֶׁת אֲדֹנָיו אֶת עֵינֶיהָ אֶל יוֹסֵף וַתֹּאמֶר שִׁכְבָה עִמִּי׃}
}
{
	\eJ{
		And it was after these things, and his lord’s wife raised
		her eyes to Joseph and said, “Lie with me.”
	}
}
{
	\aB{So before long, the wife looks up at Joseph and goes}

	\begin{center}
	\aB{\egypt{𓈖𓎡 𓅓𓂝𓇋 𓂺}}%
	\end{center}%
	\fC{
		The Egyptian may be rendered \emph{nk n=i}, using the rather
		less than euphemistic verb \emph{nk}, “to copulate”. The Hebrew
		\hE{שִׁכְבָה עִמִּי}, by contrast, literally says only “lie with me,”
		which in no way suggests copulation on the surface.
	}
}


\Verse{8}
{
	\hJ{וַיְמָאֵן וַיֹּאמֶר אֶל אֵשֶׁת אֲדֹנָיו הֵן אֲדֹנִי לֹא יָדַע אִתִּי מַה בַּבָּיִת וְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יֶשׁ לוֹ נָתַן בְּיָדִי׃}
}
{
	\eJ{
		And he refused, and he said to his lord’s wife, “Here, my
		lord doesn’t know what he has with me in the house, and
		he’s put everything that he has in my hand.
	}
}
{
	\aB{So Joseph, being a gentleman, refuses, and he spoke to her, saying}

	\begin{center}
	\aB{\egypt{
	𓅓𓎡!

	𓈖𓃀𓇋 𓈖 𓂋𓐍
	
	𓐍𓏏 𓈖𓃀𓏏 𓅓 𓉐𓏤!

	𓂧𓇋 𓐍𓏏 𓈖𓃀𓏏 𓅓 𓂝𓇋! 𓂺
	}}%
	\end{center}%
	\fC{
		Very roughly, and I do mean roughly, “Here my lord
		doesn’t know what he has put everything in my hand.”
		Punctuation omitted to maintain at least a modicum of
		propriety.
	}
}

Make it grammatical egyptian, but keep the ejaculating penis at the end, don't change my footnotes, JUST change the egyptian.
EOF
